  "dct_description_sm": [
    "These data were collected to quantify dissolved inorganic carbon and methane fluxes in a small Arctic river and characterize the associated seasonal variations. In addition, the data supported the development of the lake-ice pump conceptual model, which investigated the movement of dissolved inorganic carbon and methane across a connected lake, river, and coastal ocean continuum. This dataset supports the PhD thesis of Samantha F. Jones at the University of Calgary (2025)."
